# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify header rules.
#
# Two of these are load-bearing for WebMCP and one is a convenience:
#
#   Origin-Trial          the Chrome origin-trial token for THIS origin. Tokens
#                         are per-origin and do not cover subdomains, so a
#                         preview deployment needs its own. The <meta> tag in
#                         index.html carries the same token, because some CDNs
#                         strip one or the other and the tag is the one that
#                         actually survives an asset router answering before any
#                         middleware runs.
#   Origin-Agent-Cluster  `?0` makes document.modelContext vanish outright, and
#                         so does any use of document.domain. Pinned to ?1.
#   Cache-Control         the game is a folder of ES modules; a stale one is a
#                         confusing bug rather than a fast page.

/*
  Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?1
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Origin-Trial: REPLACE_WITH_THE_TOKEN_FOR_THIS_ORIGIN
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/
  Origin-Trial: REPLACE_WITH_THE_TOKEN_FOR_THIS_ORIGIN
  Cache-Control: no-cache
